course: dictionary
lesson: 3801
title: The forearm
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The forearm is the part of your arm between your elbow and your wrist. Rest one hand on the other forearm and you can feel it. It is a noun, so it names a part of the body you can point to.
explain: «Bend your arm and feel the biceps at the front go hard as it pulls the forearm up; straighten it and the triceps at the back pulls it down again.» The sentence tells you the forearm moves when muscles pull on it. Swap in your meaning: "the part between the elbow and the wrist gets pulled up" still makes sense.
explain: «Your arm is a chain of bones from the shoulder to the fingertips: ... two forearm bones and then a hand packed with small bones.» Here the forearm comes between the upper arm and the hand. The clues show where it sits.
explain: Forearm also has a rare verb meaning to prepare before something happens. It is in the saying «Forewarned is forearmed», which means that if you know about a danger first, you can get ready for it. Check the sentence to see whether the word is a body part or an action.
fact: The forearm is the part of the arm between the elbow and the wrist.
fact: The forearm has two bones: the radius on the thumb side and the ulna on the little-finger side.
fact: When you turn your hand, the radius rolls over the ulna.
fact: The biceps at the front pulls the forearm up, and the triceps at the back pulls it down again.
fact: «Forewarned is forearmed» means if you know about danger first, you can prepare for it.
exercise: Where is the forearm? | *Between the elbow and the wrist | Between the shoulder and the elbow | At the very top of the arm | Inside the palm, among the small bones
exercise: When you turn your hand palm up, which bone rolls over the other? | The ulna | The collarbone | The shoulder blade | *The radius
exercise: In «Forewarned is forearmed», what does forearmed mean? | Very strong | Sent away from home | *Ready, because you were warned about the danger | Hurt in the arm
test: The biceps pulls the forearm up. Which muscle pulls it back down? | Biceps | Radius | *Triceps | Ulna
test: Which bone is on the little-finger side of the forearm? | Elbow | Biceps | *Ulna | Radius
exam: Which sentence uses forearm as a verb? | Bend your forearm to lift the cup | The forearm has two bones | I hurt my forearm on the gate | *We forearmed ourselves with a plan before the storm
